version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
abstract: >-
  Single self-contained HTML page (French UI, no external resources). An event
  is identified by its phase address E = (season, shift, machine cycle, block)
  rather than by its date. A 512-value synthetic frame is split into 16 blocks
  of 32; each block is scored with S = 0.45·max|x| + 0.35·RMS + 0.20·mean|x|
  and lights when S ≥ 0.50 (fixed threshold, never recalibrated); non-finite
  values are rejected. Deterministic seeded bursts, four preloaded memories
  and an in-page self-test. Synthetic only: not a field detector, not NASA
  evidence, not a certified product.
keywords:
  - phase address
  - educational prototype
  - block score
  - oes32
  - oes512
  - synthetic data
